<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani cotton rates up on spinners' demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistani cotton rates up on spinners' demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton rates rose on Sunday amid a rise in demand by spinners and on fear of short supply of quality stock, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Fear of supply slowing down prompted spinners to cover their future requirements,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>In the kerb market, the NIAB-78 variety was traded at 2,260 rupees ($56.19) per maund (37.32 kg), he said.  </p>
<p>Sunday's official spot rates issued by the Karachi Cotton Association in rupees per maund:</p>
<p>					   Sunday	     Previous</p>
<p>    NIAB-78 (1996/97 crop)	 2,405.00	   2,377.50</p>
<p>    K-68    (1996/97 crop)	 2,586.50	   2,570.00</p>
<p>    MNH-93  (1996/97 crop)	 2,596.50	   2,580.00</p>
<p>    ($1 = 40.22 rupees)    -- Ovais Subhani 0921-5685192</p>
